35,2,1,talk,Shion,,The wall is just plasterboard. I can hear everything. And two people use the room eleven times a fortnight.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The outside hire cost 68,000 yen. The fit-outs are 141,000 and 96,000. The numbers are clear.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,Three keyboards have crumbs! And half the fridge was empty. We are wasting so much effort cleaning.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,The only talk is by the printer. The last hard conversation was said in front of everyone. We are isolated.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Eleven callouts for equipment, none for the empty room. The tally shows the same two people dominating the space.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, the tally confirms it. Two people are hoarding the room. The noise is their fault.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, the 141,000 yen for a meeting space is high. But the 96,000 for a kitchen is cheaper.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, a kitchen means more crumbs! I don't want to clean up after everyone again.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, a kitchen brings people together. But if we are just eating, we are still strangers.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the 68,000 yen we paid outside is a waste. We should use our own space properly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, a meeting space might help, but if the wall is thin, the noise will still leak.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, a quiet room costs nothing to fit out. It just needs furniture. That is the safest financial choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, a quiet room is boring! I want to do something fun. But I don't want to clean.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, a quiet room isolates us further. We need a place to talk, not just hide.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, a quiet room reduces callouts. No equipment means no maintenance. It is the most efficient.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,I am leaning towards a quiet room. It stops the noise and the hoarding.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. The quiet room is the cheapest and least risky. I want to see the figures on paper.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I guess a quiet room is okay. As long as nobody makes a mess!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"I worry about the isolation. But if the other options are too messy, perhaps we start there.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I support the quiet room. It minimizes the hidden hours and the maintenance burden.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
