67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, I agree! No cleaning is the best part. I am happy with C.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Shion, perhaps we can add a small table for quiet reading? But I will stick with C.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, keep it simple. No extra furniture means no extra callouts. C is the answer.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,I stand by my vote for C. It solves the noise and the usage imbalance.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I stand by my vote for C. The financial risk is lowest here.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I stand by my vote for C. No mess, no stress.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,I stand by my vote for C. It is a start. We can build connection later.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I stand by my vote for C. It is the most sustainable option for our hours.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
